sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/rule54-universality--claude-opus-5-5--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Automated synthesis of a cyclic-tag emulation from the complete collision graph" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/rule54-universality> ;
    dct:description "Treat universality search as program synthesis over glider collisions. First compute the complete set of Rule 54 gliders on the standard ether up to period 120 and width 80 (de Bruijn diagrams), and the full binary collision table over all phases and gaps (outgoing gliders, phase shifts, and whether the outcome depends on the gap). Then search the collision graph for the four functional components of a Cook-style CTS emulation: stationary or slow 'tape' gliders encoding 0 and 1; a periodic left-moving 'program' stream encoding appendants; an annihilation or conversion reaction that reads the leading tape symbol; and a reaction that appends or deletes appendant material conditionally. Encode timing and spacing constraints as an SMT problem (z3, integer gaps modulo the ether period) and search for satisfying assignments that emulate a 2-appendant CTS. A solution is validated by direct simulation and then formalized as in the Rule 110 approach." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "An explicit initial configuration (ether, finite seed, periodic stream) on which Rule 54 emulates arbitrary CTS, validated by simulation and then proved in Lean. Short of that, a proof that the collision graph restricted to gliders up to the bound lacks a conditional-append reaction, which pins down what a universal construction would need." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The SMT search finds no conditional reaction among gliders up to the bound; every collision outcome is independent of the data it would need to read. That is evidence that the bound is too small or that the second (impossibility) approach is the right one." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/computation" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Compute and publish the glider catalogue with periods, velocities and phases; compare with Martínez, Adamatzky and McIntosh 2006. 2. Compute the complete binary collision table and identify collisions that are gap-sensitive, the raw material for conditional behaviour. 3. Encode CTS-emulation components as SMT constraints over glider choices and gaps; search with increasing component sizes. 4. Validate any candidate by simulating a small universal CTS for 10^7 generations and decoding." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): long-shot" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Conditional (data-reading) reactions may not exist among small gliders; the search may need structures no one has catalogued." ;
    skos:note "Tool: cellular-automaton-simulation" ;
    skos:note "Tool: glider-collision-search" ;
    skos:note "Tool: smt-solver" ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-21> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-19> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-20> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chaos.2005.05.013> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.25088/ComplexSystems.15.1.1> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/z3prover/z3> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/rule54-universality> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Is Rule 54 computationally universal?" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chaos.2005.05.013> dct:title "Phenomenology of glider collisions in cellular automaton Rule 54 and associated logical gates" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Martínez, Adamatzky and McIntosh 2006, Phenomenology of glider collisions in cellular automaton Rule 54 and associated logical gates (Chaos, Solitons & Fractals 28:100). The DOI listed in problems.json resolves to a different paper." .
  <https://doi.org/10.25088/ComplexSystems.15.1.1> dct:title "Universality in Elementary Cellular Automata" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Cook 2004, template for the CTS-emulation architecture" .
  <https://github.com/z3prover/z3> dct:bibliographicCitation "Z3 SMT solver for the timing-constraint search" .
}

